.nh
.TH "PB-PREVIEW-STOP" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-preview-stop - Stop a temporary preview


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb preview stop <preview> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop one temporary preview, selected by its ID or name, and withdraw its published access. Other
previews and durable tunnels are not affected. The command prints the stopped preview, or with
--json the stopped resource. pb preview delete does the same.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for stop

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the stopped canonical preview resource as JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb preview stop preview_abc123
  pb preview stop preview_abc123 --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-preview(1)\fP
